  ! flagged   ✓ ok   ? unknown   · reported, never flagged
  · 100% of dev Cases carry more than one behavior tag — a failure in those
    Cases testifies about every tag it carries, so per-behavior attribution is
    shared. (Heuristic: a tag is a label, not a claim about what a Case
    exercises. Reported, not flagged: there is no principled threshold for
    this.)
  ✓ 5 distinct behaviors on 132 of 132 dev Cases
  ✓ every behavior has at least 5 dev Cases (core.MinClusterCases)
  ! "billing" is carried by 52% of dev Cases
  ✓ the holdout has 28 Cases (20 is the minimum for a meaningful interval at
    validate)
  ? attribution_observed is unknown: no --value-run-id given

1 of 5 checks flagged.  If these tags are behaviors you would fix separately:
  - split "billing" into the behaviors you would act on separately
  - re-run with --value-run-id <id> to see which behaviors a run actually
    attributed

What each number claims: docs/what-the-numbers-mean.md
Designing evals: docs/evaluation-design.md

